From b851afe42c3debd5beb4b3e1131236394eb0cf48 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hoangvu12 <hggaming91@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 23:17:07 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] Child chats report back to the chat that made them

When an agent hands work to subagents or side chats, each child's answer
comes back to it on its own when the child's turn ends. The parent never
has to poll, and the person never has to nudge either side.

- A report shows as a compact row on a card that opens the child, with the
  first two lines of what it said when it finished or asks something.
  Reports that land together share one card. A spawn of one chat sits on
  the same card.
- A parent that is free hears after a short window of 3 seconds, so
  children finishing together wake it once. A busy parent reads what came
  meanwhile as one message when its turn ends. Nothing waits on a slow or
  stuck sibling.
- Under the reports, for the agent only, Zeron notes which children still
  work for the parent, how long since each was asked and last did
  anything, a question waiting on it, and long runs of back and forth with
  the person away.
- A child that is asked something, fails, is stopped or sends a message
  mid task reaches the parent the same way, in order. A Stop says who made
  it, so a stopped child never reads as finished, and only the person's
  reads as theirs. A steer that stops a turn to be read at once is no
  Stop: that turn goes on, and reports when it ends.
- Each report goes by a key kept in the parent's chat, on the message its
  turn answered (not a message sent after it). A stop's report has its own
  key, so the end of the work it cut still reports. A report that couldn't
  be queued goes on the next try. A restart, a crash or a child on another
  device loses none and repeats none. An archived parent keeps its reports
  until restored.
- A parent reads Waiting while its children work, and its spawn rows take
  how each child ended from its report. A child on another device that
  has reported is never listed as "sent, not started".
